A||||5||jch82||Need a new muffler??||||5||
Z||000000||jch82||10-01-2001||02:03 AM||||Well my exhaust has been sounding really bad lately and tonite it decided that it wanted to get REALLY loud. I'm almost positive it's my muffler but just wanted to make sure. How can I tell if it is my muffler and not just a hole in the exhaust itself?? If it was just a hole, then would it still get loud?? All I did was back out of my friends driveway and take off....Then it just takes a $hit...Thanks!<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||BlackARROW||10-01-2001||03:13 AM||||It's starting to get colder here, so you can see exhaust leak very easily  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>Other than that, I use my hears and hands to find leaks (just passing over).  Start it when motor is cool, and by the time it will get too hot, you will have already found it. <P>Anywhere along the whole exhaust line, but after the muffler, a hole would get loud. After the muffler, it would just leak and maybe rattles - but not get loud.<P>If you have to change your muffler, maybe it would be a good time to look for a new performance one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  If it's the cat. - go straight pipe baby  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Good Luck<P><P>------------------<BR>BlackARROW &gt;&gt;--&gt;<BR>Gadgeteered Fiero 2M4 '85<BR>"Get your groove on"||||reg||1
Z||000002||sloth85GT||10-01-2001||03:14 AM||||Wow, your car looks exactly like mine minus the wheels, is it an 85 GT as well? <P>Anyways regarding your question, I had a similar problem, I looked underneath the car, and saw a cracked pipe. Feel if you have any exhaust coming out of your tips. If not, then it's a pipe. Check your pipes first because in most situations, a pipe chunk can be cut out and a new piece welded in, it's not the best fix in the world, but it works, that's what I did.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">     <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Svyn||10-01-2001||10:48 AM||||On this note, what do you guys suggest for a high flow , weld in muffler w/o changing pipes? Mine has decided to let go at the seam so I am due for one aswell. I can't stand the noise so I am driving my SC =).<P>------------------<BR>-Dale Clark<BR>86' Fiero SE<BR>99' Dodge Durango SLT+<BR>92' Ford ThunderBird SuperCoupe||||reg||1
Z||000004||jch82||10-01-2001||11:29 AM||||Thanks Everyone! I will check out my pipes when I get out of college. So it could be the cat that went out too?? If that's the case, then straight pipe it is! I just can't stand the sound and it only happened last night. Just driving the 2mi back to my house was enough....<P>Yes mine is an 85gt! Picked her up from Saginaw, MI back in April. She has been running strong ever since. Thanks!<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82_1.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000005||jch82||10-01-2001||06:29 PM||||Well, problem solved! It was the cat that went out. One side rusted right off....I ended up putting a straight pipe on. Only cost me $7. $4 for the pipe from autozone and $3 for three clamps....Easy fix!! Thanks<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
